---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
---

<DocLayout title="Studio Rigs & Presets">
  <h1>Parametric Studio Rigs & Presets</h1>
  <p>
    Scene Light Manager (SLM) features pre-calibrated, interactive studio lighting rigs. Spawning a rig automatically builds collection hierarchies, empty control handles, tracking targets, and constraints to let you manipulate professional setups instantly.
  </p>

  <hr class="my-8 border-white/5" />

  <h2>── 1. Spawning a Lighting Rig ──</h2>
  <p>
    Under the <strong>LIGHTS</strong> tab of the SLM sidebar, click the <strong>Presets</strong> dropdown. Selecting any rig preset automatically triggers the following pipeline:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-xs mb-6">
    <li>Generates a dedicated collection named after the rig category.</li>
    <li>Spawns a tracking Target empty at the 3D Cursor.</li>
    <li>Applies <code>Track To</code> constraints to the spawned lights, forcing them to look at the target.</li>
    <li>Spawns empty controller handles for global offsets, rotation, and distance parameters.</li>
  </ul>

  <hr class="my-8 border-white/5" />

  <h2>── 2. Built-in Rig Presets ──</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs mb-6">
    <div class="bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/5 p-4 rounded-xl hover:border-white/10 hover:bg-white/[0.04] transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col gap-3 group">
      <div class="aspect-square w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg bg-black/40 border border-white/5">
        <img 
          src="/light_rigs_images/Rig%2001%20(3-Point).webp" 
          alt="3-Point Light Rig" 
          class="w-full h-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105" 
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong class="text-white text-sm block mb-1">3-Point Light Rig (Classic Setup)</strong>
        <p class="text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
          The gold standard for portraiture and product rendering. Spawns a Key light (primary exposure), a soft Fill light (shadow balance), and a Rim/Back light (separates subject silhouettes from dark backgrounds).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/5 p-4 rounded-xl hover:border-white/10 hover:bg-white/[0.04] transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col gap-3 group">
      <div class="aspect-square w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg bg-black/40 border border-white/5">
        <img 
          src="/light_rigs_images/Rig%2002%20(Studio%20Duo).webp" 
          alt="Studio Duo" 
          class="w-full h-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105" 
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong class="text-white text-sm block mb-1">Studio Duo</strong>
        <p class="text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
          A clean, mirror-like dual-light configuration flanking both sides of the subject. Highly suited for minimalist layouts, vehicles, and clean product design presentations.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/5 p-4 rounded-xl hover:border-white/10 hover:bg-white/[0.04] transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col gap-3 group">
      <div class="aspect-square w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg bg-black/40 border border-white/5">
        <img 
          src="/light_rigs_images/Rig%2003%20(Warm-Cool).webp" 
          alt="Warm-Cool Split" 
          class="w-full h-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105" 
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong class="text-white text-sm block mb-1">Warm-Cool Split</strong>
        <p class="text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
          Sets up opposing temperature light colors (amber/orange vs. cool blue) to create dramatic color contrasts. Fits stylized cinematic concepts or sci-fi environments.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/5 p-4 rounded-xl hover:border-white/10 hover:bg-white/[0.04] transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col gap-3 group">
      <div class="aspect-square w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg bg-black/40 border border-white/5">
        <img 
          src="/light_rigs_images/Rig%2004%20(Dramatic%20Rim).webp" 
          alt="Dramatic Rim" 
          class="w-full h-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105" 
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong class="text-white text-sm block mb-1">Dramatic Rim</strong>
        <p class="text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
          Arranges intense directional lights behind and adjacent to the subject, casting hard silhouettes and tracing outline shapes, leaving the camera-facing surfaces dark.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/5 p-4 rounded-xl hover:border-white/10 hover:bg-white/[0.04] transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col gap-3 group">
      <div class="aspect-square w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg bg-black/40 border border-white/5">
        <img 
          src="/light_rigs_images/Rig%2005%20(Butterfly).webp" 
          alt="Butterfly" 
          class="w-full h-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105" 
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong class="text-white text-sm block mb-1">Butterfly (Beauty Setup)</strong>
        <p class="text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
          Spawns the main emitter directly above and slightly in front of the camera path. Minimizes surface wrinkles and textures, classic in high-fashion modeling renders.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/5 p-4 rounded-xl hover:border-white/10 hover:bg-white/[0.04] transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col gap-3 group">
      <div class="aspect-square w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg bg-black/40 border border-white/5">
        <img 
          src="/light_rigs_images/Rig%2006%20(Double%20Sun).webp" 
          alt="Double Sun" 
          class="w-full h-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105" 
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong class="text-white text-sm block mb-1">Double Sun</strong>
        <p class="text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
          Mimics a binary star environment, generating stylized double directional highlights and shadow structures. Ideal for sci-fi desert landscapes and artistic concepts.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <hr class="my-8 border-white/5" />

  <h2>── 3. Controlling Rigs (Parametric Sliders) ──</h2>
  <p>
    Selecting a rig's collection or empty controller handle in the SLM list opens the <strong>Rig Properties</strong> sidebar panel, containing specialized sliders:
  </p>

  <ul class="space-y-4 mb-6">
    <li class="bg-white/[0.01] border border-white/5 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs">
      <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Global Scale & Distance:</strong>
      Adjusts the distance of all emitters from the target, scaling the entire rig radius symmetrically.
    </li>
    <li class="bg-white/[0.01] border border-white/5 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs">
      <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Base Energy & Contrast:</strong>
      Base Energy acts as a global exposure multiplier for the entire rig. Contrast scales the energy ratio between Key and Fill lights to control shadow hardness.
    </li>
    <li class="bg-white/[0.01] border border-white/5 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs">
      <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Height & Tracking Height:</strong>
      Height raises or lowers the emitters vertically. Tracking Height moves the look-at target empty up or down to concentrate lights on specific features.
    </li>
  </ul>
</DocLayout>
